# Lineup-classifier training data (exported by scripts/export-lineup-dataset.mjs)
# training-data/ is machine-local (frames cache, manifests, exports) EXCEPT the
# hand-made label files, which are the only ground truth and travel with git
# (Tom, 2026-10-18 — the terminal labels were lost once in August, and in
# October each machine held labels the other lacked). A directory ignore
# cannot be re-included, hence the /* form.
/training-data/*
!/training-data/terminal-labels.json
!/training-data/lineup-crosswalk-hand.json
!/training-data/lineup-dark-labels.json
!/training-data/tag-corrections.json
!/training-data/dark-detections-verdict.json
/.vscode/

# Classifier-results report: ~75 MB of regenerated artifacts (three HTML pages
# plus ~5k thumbnails). Deployed to Cloud Storage instead, self-contained —
# npm run deploy:classifier-results
public/classifier-results/
/nono-claude.sh
